    "name": "Fin",
    "pageid": 273,
    "summary": "Fin is a male SeaWing prince who was introduced in Talons of Power. He is one of the thirty-two sons of King Gill and Queen Coral. He currently resides in the Deep Palace with his brothers.\n\n\n== Personality ==\nFin seems to be one of the kinder or more considerate of Turtle's brothers, as he showed concern for Turtle when told about Anemone's soul. He seemed cautious of animus magic, and appears to have a sense of humor, such as when he joked about bringing all his brothers with him on the mapping mission.\n\n\n== Biography ==\n\n\n=== The Dragonet Prophecy ===\n\n\n==== The Lost Heir ====\nFin was indirectly mentioned when Anemone said she has lots of brothers, but she could not play with them because Coral believed they play too rough.\n\n\n=== The Jade Mountain Prophecy ===\n\n\n==== Moon Rising ====\nFin was indirectly mentioned when Turtle told Tsunami that she had thirty-two brothers.\n\n\n==== Talons of Power ====\nFin was first introduced when Turtle was going to warn his mother about Anemone. Fin saw Turtle and wondered why he had left Jade Mountain Academy to return to the Deep Palace. He referred to the academy as a \"fancy hugging school.\" Turtle explained about Anemone, then told him to gather their brothers and take them...",
