    "name": "Kinkajou",
    "pageid": 400,
    "summary": "Kinkajou is a female RainWing dragonet and the main protagonist of Book Seventeen. Formerly a captive of the NightWings on the NightWing island, she attended Jade Mountain Academy as a member of the Jade Winglet before her disappearance.\n\n\n== Description ==\nKinkajou's scales are typically kept at bright colors, such as pink and yellow. She has a long neck, gigantic dark green eyes, tiny claws, and a diamond-shaped snout. She is small and is the same size as Anemone despite being slightly older than her.\n\n\n== Personality ==\nKinkajou is bouncy, snarky, fierce, bright, immature, mischievous, and quick to anger in difficult situations. She smiles often, but can become dangerous when her friends are threatened. According to Carnelian, she is noisy and talks all day. She looks at problems as something she can solve, instead of thinking \"everything is hopeless.\" She runs straight toward danger without thinking first and is annoyed when she misses the action and heroism. Kinkajou wants to be a dragon others will notice and remember and does not like the idea of being unimportant. According to her, she has spent nearly her whole life waking up dragons who would rather be sleeping than talking to...",
