    "name": "Lagoon (L1)",
    "pageid": 411,
    "summary": "(Not to be confused with Lagoon, Queen Coral's cook who was introduced in The Lost Heir.)\n\nLagoon was an adult female SeaWing queen who was introduced in Darkstalker. She was the first victim of the Royal SeaWing Massacre, killed by her brother and animus Albatross, who sent a knife into her throat. Before her death, she ruled over the SeaWing tribe with her husband, King Humpback, during Darkstalker's era. She was the mother of Splash and the great-aunt of Fathom and Pearl.\n\n\n== Description ==\nLagoon had sapphire-blue scales and blue wings. She wore a crown, had a small, refined frown, and a glittering smile.\n\n\n== Personality ==\nLagoon was cold, poised, blunt, mean, divisive, sinister, scrutinizing, and tended to either ignore or order around those she considered insignificant. She spoke silkily and was skilled at negotiating peace. She felt prejudice towards the lower classes, and believed in the higher importance of royal dragons.\n\n\n== Biography ==\n\n\n=== Pre-Series ===\nLagoon was next in line to rule the SeaWings, along with her sister, Princess Sapphire. She often liked to tease her brother, Albatross. One time, while teasing Albatross with Sapphire, Albatross accidentally enchanted a clam...",
