    "name": "Linden",
    "pageid": 427,
    "summary": "Linden was an adult female LeafWing who was featured in A Guide to the Dragon World. She was the mother of Belladonna and the grandmother of Sundew. She was formerly Queen Sequoia's best general during the Tree Wars before breaking off and becoming the founder and leader of the PoisonWings. Before her death, she resided in the PoisonWing village and had the ability of leafspeak.\n\n\n== Personality ==\nLinden was brave, stubborn, vengeful, confident, and fiercely loyal to Sequoia before founding the PoisonWings. According to Sequoia, she was careful and a good general.\n\n\n== Biography ==\n\n\n=== Pre-Series ===\nLinden was Sequoia's best general until the end of the Tree Wars. When the queen ordered a retreat, Linden refused to back down - this insubordination led her to break off from the tribe and create the PoisonWings. Despite this, Linden would exchange letters with Sequoia throughout the rest of her life.\nShe used her leafspeak to begin making the PoisonWing Village. Her daughter, Belladonna, would hatch after Linden broke off from the SapWings and she would arrange Belladonna's marriage with Hemlock.\nLinden was eventually killed by a gympie-gympie stinging tree while running a drill with a group...",
