    "name": "Swamp",
    "pageid": 766,
    "summary": "Swamp was an adult male MudWing who was introduced in Assassin. He served as a MudWing general during the war and was one of the MudWings located in Blister's hideout at the time. He was executed by Blister after being framed for the death of Commander Tempest.\n\n\n== Personality ==\nSwamp was described to have a short temper and was easily agitated. He was extremely loyal to his tribe and was quick to point the blame at others.\n\n\n== Biography ==\n\n\n=== Winglets ===\n\n\n==== Assassin ====\nGeneral Swamp, along with several MudWing soldiers, was in a meeting with Princess Blister, King Gill, and Commander Tempest to discuss a plan for the SandWing throne. After dropping his weapons, he and his troops entered a tent for a meeting with Blister's forces. Commander Tempest was assassinated by Deathbringer a short moment after; the guards stationed outside the tent were blamed due to how she was killed by a MudWing spear and how no one else was around to witness it other than the then-unconscious Quickstrike. This led to a note accusing the SeaWings of making a secret deal with Blister. Swamp stated that if his soldiers were punished, he would revoke his alliance with the latter princess. Seeing as the MudWings...",
