    "name": "Vengeance",
    "pageid": 882,
    "summary": "Vengeance was an adult male NightWing who was introduced in The Hidden Kingdom. He formerly served as a guard for the NightWings until he was killed by being thrown into a lava pool as punishment for disobeying Queen Battlewinner's orders.\n\n\n== Description ==\nVengeance was large and had a horribly deformed snout; a twisting scar that closed one of his nostrils, multiple melted scales, and oozing bubbles of deformed skin along his jawline caused by Splendor's venom. He breathed in a loud, snuffly way and had a hoarse, wet voice. According to Fierceteeth, he was hideous even before his injury.\n\n\n== Personality ==\nAccording to Morrowseer, Vengeance would love to practice killing other dragons, and Quickstrike stated that he was unintelligent. He was vengeful, greedy, and disobedient. Vengeance was selfish, pushing away other guards to escape first.\n\n\n== Biography ==\n\n\n=== The Dragonet Prophecy ===\n\n\n==== The Hidden Kingdom ====\nIt was mentioned early in the book that RainWings were missing, including Queen Splendor. When the dragonets were searching for Orchid, they found a dying sloth with a nasty bite on it. Later, they heard something out at night that sounded like a monster. They heard bones crunching...",
