    "name": "Waterfall",
    "pageid": 104989,
    "summary": "Waterfall was a female SeaWing animus who was mentioned in The Hybrid Prince. She was a descendant of Fathom and Indigo. During her life, she ended up trapped on the Dungeon Isle, where she used her magic to make it a better place for the dragons that were also trapped there.\n\n\n== Description ==\nWaterfall's statue was abstractly carved with blue-gray stone and had shells that shimmered deep blue, pale green, and silver embedded along the lines of her wings and her cheekbones like the iridescent aquatic patterns on Turtle and Tsunami. The statue had a serene face.\n\n\n== Biography ==\n\n\n=== Pre-Series ===\nWhen Waterfall came to the Dungeon Isle, she had Blob with her. She created the Court of Refuge, a palace that can change shape to fit the needs of its residents. She also enchanted orchards to grow fruits and water sources to never run dry.\n\n\n=== The Forgotten Isles Prophecy ===\n\n\n==== The Hybrid Prince ====\nSora and Umber saw a statue of Waterfall in the Court of Refuge, leading to Beryl explaining who she was and what she did for the prisoners of the Isle.\nLater, after Umber was injured following his attempt at crossing the Barrier, he met Paua, a descendant of Waterfall. Paua said that Waterfall tried...",
